## Sequence Diagram

The following diagram illustrates the asynchronous message processing flow within the Broker.

```plantuml
@startuml
autonumber

box "Application Logic" #White
    actor "Client / Main App" as Client
end box

box "MOM (Message Oriented Middleware)" #LightBlue
    participant "Broker" as Broker
    participant "MessageContainer" as Queue
    participant "Broker Thread\n(Async Loop)" as Thread
end box

box "External System" #LightGray
    participant "HR / API Endpoint" as API
end box

== Initialization & Startup ==

Client -> Broker: new Broker(url)
Client -> Broker: start()
activate Broker

create Thread
Broker -> Thread: start()
activate Thread

Broker --> Client: return (non-blocking)
deactivate Broker

note right of Thread: Loop runs asynchronously\nchecks queue every 1s

== Message Production ==

Client -> Broker: send_message(message)
activate Broker
Broker -> Queue: push_message(message)
activate Queue
Queue --> Broker
deactivate Queue
Broker --> Client
deactivate Broker

== Message Consumption (Background) ==

loop while running
    Thread -> Thread: sleep(1)
    
    Thread -> Queue: get_message()
    activate Queue
    Queue --> Thread: message
    deactivate Queue

    alt message is not None
        Thread -> API: POST (JSON payload)
        activate API
        
        alt HTTP Success (200 OK)
            API --> Thread: Response {success: True}
            Thread -> Queue: delete_message(message)
            activate Queue
            Queue --> Thread
            deactivate Queue
            Thread -> Thread: log info
        else HTTP Error / Exception
            API --> Thread: Error / 500 / Timeout
            deactivate API
            Thread -> Thread: log error
            note right: Message remains in Queue\nfor retry
        end
    end
end

== Shutdown ==

Client -> Broker: stop()
activate Broker
Broker -> Thread: _running = False
Broker -> Thread: join()
deactivate Thread
destroy Thread
Broker --> Client
deactivate Broker

@enduml
```
